/*
RMSTEST_33a - is create_terrain actually locked to <TERRAIN_GENERATION>
CLAUDE.md tracked debt: validate()'s RMS0304 wrong-section check

NOT a Sec.15 item. This is the blocker on one of the two Sec.8 checks that
shipped unbuilt, and it is a game question, so it rides along with this batch.
Skip it if the sitting runs long - nothing else depends on it.

QUESTION
validate() has nine of eleven Sec.8 checks live. RMS0304, the wrong-section
check, is not built, and the build log records why: we do not know WHICH
commands are actually section-locked. language.json assigns every command a
section, but that field records where a command BELONGS in well-formed RMS, and
nobody has established that the engine enforces it. Those are different claims
and the check needs the second one.

Getting this wrong is expensive in a specific direction. If the engine happily
runs a misplaced command, RMS0304 would flag working maps as broken - the exact
false-positive class that BUG-002 and BUG-005 have already cost this project
three rounds of work. So the check stays unbuilt until measured, which is the
right call and is why this script exists rather than a plausible argument.

METHOD
create_terrain, placed in <OBJECTS_GENERATION> instead of
<TERRAIN_GENERATION>. Everything else is a minimal working map. The terrain
histogram is a clean binary: either SNOW appears or it does not.

The <TERRAIN_GENERATION> header is present but EMPTY, so the section exists and
only the command's placement is wrong. That matters - an absent section is a
different test, and an absent <ELEVATION_GENERATION> is already known to be an
error-severity condition that crashes in play.

GENERATE AT NORMAL (200), any player count.

PREDICTIONS, RECORDED BEFORE THE RUN
1. SNOW appears at roughly its declared share. The engine reads the script as a
   flat statement list and section headers are mostly organisational. If so,
   RMS0304 must NOT be built as an error for this command, and probably should
   be info at most.
2. SNOW does not appear at all. The section genuinely gates execution, RMS0304
   is worth building as a warning, and this command can be listed as locked.
3. Generation fails or the map comes back malformed. Also an answer, and the
   strongest possible argument for the check - but record exactly what "fails"
   looked like, because a crash and a silent no-op need different diagnostic
   text.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT ESTABLISH, and it is the reason to run 33b as well
One command answering one way says nothing about the others. There is no reason
to expect a uniform rule: the engine may hoist some commands, ignore others, and
enforce a third group. RMS0304 needs a PER-COMMAND list, and this batch starts it
with two entries rather than pretending to finish it. Extend the same pattern to
create_land in <TERRAIN_GENERATION>, and to the <ELEVATION_GENERATION> commands,
before the check is built.

READ IT WITH
  python probe_scenario.py "<scenario>"
  The default terrain histogram is the whole reading. Look for SNOW.

ONE RUN IS ENOUGH if the answer is clean. Run a second only if SNOW appears at a
share far off the declared 10 percent, which would suggest the command ran but
under different rules.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain GRASS

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>


<TERRAIN_GENERATION>


<OBJECTS_GENERATION>

  /* DELIBERATELY IN THE WRONG SECTION. This is the test. */
  create_terrain SNOW
  {
    base_terrain GRASS
    land_percent 10
    number_of_clumps 10
    set_scale_by_groups
  }

<CONNECTION_GENERATION>
